{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M72R7PH0H0X1K5"},{"$ref":"1M72R7PH0H0X1NY"},{"$ref":"1M72R7PH0H0X1QS"},{"$ref":"1M72R7PH0H0X1VC"}],"opens":"An expression stays what it was: calls of functions given what they take, nested, a graph of functions. A function says what it gives one of three ways: as an expression of other functions, as a pattern of facts, or as code handed only values, so its purity is what it is given and not a promise. The functions glass ships, with good names, are the 15 natives of today written so; the engine's own part shrinks to what working out a pattern needs.","restsOn":["The pattern form grounded in the nineteen cases","A name for the pattern form","Code functions run only where components may"],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M72R7PH0H0X1WK","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"Expressions are calls, functions give three ways"}
{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M72R7PH0H0X1A7"},{"$ref":"1M72R7PH0H0X1GP"},{"$ref":"1M72R7PH0H0X1K5"},{"$ref":"1M72R7PH0H0X1NY"},{"$ref":"1M72R7PH0H0X1Q1"}],"opens":"Taken from Datomic: a holon read as facts, holon, key and value, every value it holds usable; a pattern is clauses over them, with variables shared between clauses as the links, not and or, rules that recurse over what the field holds and so always end, and what it gives with counts and folds, then order and a window. Held as JSON in a function's body. The engine plans it and can say which index served each clause. Proposed to be called pattern; the name is the author's.","restsOn":["The kernel prototype and its nineteen cases, 689b350","The field as arrays with its indexes"],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M72R7PH0H0X1WM","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"A pattern of facts, the low language of functions"}
{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M72R7PH0H0X1F9"},{"$ref":"1M72R7PH0H0X1GP"}],"opens":"Four indexes, each the same facts in another order: by holon, by key, by key and value, and by value, the last being what refers to a holon. Each is derived, the same from the same commit, so it can be checked, cached and shipped as blocks named by their hash; a store's top, what nothing in it holds, becomes a fact, and the field's top no longer needs everything read.","restsOn":["Where an index's blocks stand in the format","Which wholes keep an index of their own, left open in the store brief"],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M72R7PH0H0X1WN","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"Indexes that can be understood, shipped by the store"}
{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M72R7PH0H0X1F9"}],"opens":"Every id interned to a number, edges in and out packed as arrays, 1.3 MB for 174,606 edges and built in about 100 ms: a store's level in 1.3 ms against 273 ms through the kernel as written. The meaning stays the kernel's; only how it is worked out changes, the cases proving nothing moved.","restsOn":["The engine's field rebuilt on it, with today's natives and the cases over it"],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M72R7PH0H0X1WP","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"The field as arrays"}
{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M72R7PH0H0X1GP"}],"opens":"A word's lexeme is its text normalised, lower case with the 's let go, so the lexicon stores one fact three times: in the text, in the reference, in the list rewritten at each new word. As a function, lexeme of text, and the value index over it, it holds nothing the words do not say. A Term, a word holding a reference, stays a deliberate thing of its own.","restsOn":["The value index over a function","A store change: 3,681 lexemes and the lexicon taken out, a field gone from 67,018 words"],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M72R7PH0H0X1WQ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"The lexicon as a function"}
{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M72R7PH0H0X1VC"}],"opens":"The field holds the expression as data, never a string. Text is a face of it, a print and parse pair: find and where, pipes, the address, the CLI. In the reader it is drawn as itself, chips, clauses and the variables that link them, each edit writing the data, the formula said at the top and changed where it stands.","restsOn":["The written form settled from the grounded cases"],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M72R7PH0H0X1WR","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"An expression drawn as itself"}
{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M72R7PH0H0X1F9"}],"opens":"From The Value of Values: the store never rewrites, so the field at a commit is a value, and at is working an expression out against that value, as Datomic's as-of, not a verb that reaches back. It asks commits that say what they changed, which the log does not yet give.","restsOn":["Commits that name what they changed, read by the engine"],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M72R7PH0H0X1WS","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"The field as a value at a commit"}
